{"duration_api_ms":42237,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a","total_cost_usd":0.36762680000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":16,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24008,"cache_read_input_tokens":390194,"output_tokens":4873,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":273},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24008,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":643,"cache_read_input_tokens":55739,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":523},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":4873,"cacheReadInputTokens":390194,"cacheCreationInputTokens":24008,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.36762680000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":273,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":24008,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":8,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've fixed the three problems from the rejection, and the sdkjs-common oracle now passes with 6 of 6 suites (10066/10323 assertions, about 130 s). Both acceptance commands pass: `unit.sh` gives 178 passed and 1 skipped, and `lint:check` has 0 errors and 1 warning that was already there. The work is committed as `211e06a`.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **color-mods runs by default.** It passes only if the count is exactly 9766/10023 and the failing tests are exactly the 11 known names. Any other result fails the oracle, whether the suite gets fixed or gets worse, and the runner prints what it expected. The 11 names are listed in a `known` table in `.theseus/oracle/sdkjs-common-run.cjs`. The local skips and the `ORACLE_ALL=1` switch are gone.\n- **chartEx-serialize runs by default too.** It passes only if it still times out at 120 s, which I confirmed on this run.\n- **The runner fails when no suite runs.** It prints `FAIL no suite matched` and exits 1; I checked this with a filter that matches nothing.\n- **The `sdkjs-common.sh` header now describes the real suite list,** including the two known-broken suites.\n- **The card, the packet's Executor log and the friction line are updated.**\n\n**Decisions:**\n- **I kept the full 120 s timeout for chartEx-serialize.** A shorter timeout would prove less, and since the suite runs alongside the others, the whole oracle still takes about 130 s.\n- **A timeout check has a limit:** it can't tell a hang from a very slow run. This is written on the card.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- When a suite is known to be broken, pin its exact failure in a test instead of skipping it. That way the oracle notices both a fix and a regression.\n- A suite pinned on a timeout adds about 2 minutes to every oracle run.","ttft_ms":1936,"type":"result","duration_ms":319057,"uuid":"0ed3451f-6197-4d5a-bf27-796a24ab0ffa","ttft_stream_ms":911,"time_to_request_ms":316,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":165,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":23,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":16,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":12,"query_setup":4,"auto_mo